impact: an agent reviewing its own staged work no longer has to explain files
  it has not staged

@note +196 confidence=0.85
why: git's own `index` line gives abbreviated hashes, so a document mixing the
  two sources had 7-character hashes for tracked files and 40-character ones
  for untracked files. Staleness comparison is prefix-based either way; this
  is purely so the generated file reads consistently.
