@note +479..481 kind=intent risk=medium confidence=0.9
why: This is the parser half of a round-trip bug. `parseUnifiedDiff` fills
  `oldPath` from the `--- a/path` line of every diff, including plain
  modifications, the serializer then wrote `from=<same path>`, and re-parsing
  that file inferred `renamed` from the presence of `from=`. A file that was
  only edited came back as a rename.
